  "seoBody": "<h2>Why per-user pricing is a bad fit for small field firms</h2><p>Most of the established tools in this space charge per user. That model makes sense for the vendor — every new engineer is incremental cost on the licence, regardless of how much value the firm extracts.</p><p>From the small-firm side, the maths is the other way round. The first engineer to use the tool is the one who decides whether it sticks. If each additional engineer adds another per-user charge, the small firm either holds rollout back (defeating the point) or pays per-user for engineers who barely use the tool.</p><h2>How Quickler is priced</h2><p>One pound per completed report. Unlimited users, managers, admins and workflows on every bundle, so adding staff is free.</p><p>[[price:bundles]].</p><p>Over 500 reports a month, contact us for custom pricing. There is a 14-day free trial with no card required. Billed monthly by UK Direct Debit, with other payment rails added as firms in new markets come on board. No setup fee. Quickler runs on any inspection or checklist, not just one trade, and <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">works in any country</a> WhatsApp does.</p><h2>What that looks like in practice</h2><p><strong>A firm completing around a hundred reports a month</strong> pays £100/month on Quickler 100, with unlimited engineers covered and unlimited workflows included.</p><p><strong>A firm completing a few hundred reports a month</strong> pays £250/month on Quickler 250, again flat, with no per-seat charge however many engineers run the checks.</p><p>We deliberately avoid quoting other vendors' specific prices here because their tiers and discounts change. Check their own pages for current numbers.</p><h2>Where Quickler is not the right pick</h2><p>If you need a full field service management platform — scheduling, dispatching, quoting, invoicing, asset tracking — Quickler is not the right tool. A full field service suite is the right pick when you want one platform to run the whole business. Quickler is for firms whose problem is specifically the compliance-paperwork half.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/alternatives.html\">Where Quickler fits and where it does not</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What if I add more engineers?</h3><p>Adding staff is free. Every bundle includes unlimited users, managers, admins and workflows. You only pay per report, so the number of engineers never changes the price. If you complete more reports than your bundle, move up a bundle. No per-engineer charges, no surprise bills.</p><h3>Is there a setup fee?</h3><p>No setup fee on standard bundles. For bespoke onboarding (custom workflow templates beyond the standard EICR, CP12, van check and structural set), one-off setup is quoted per project.</p><h3>Is there a free trial?</h3><p>Yes. There is a 14-day free trial with no card required. Sign up at app.quickler.co/signup. The trial lets a real engineer run a real check and a real report comes out the other end. Setup to first live workflow typically takes under a week.</p><h3>What if we only need it for three months of the year?</h3><p>Bundles are monthly and you can cancel at any time. Data export on cancellation is supported on request.</p><h3>Do you do per-engineer pricing if we prefer it?</h3><p>No. Per report is the deliberate model: adding staff is free, which removes the disincentive to roll the tool out across the whole team. If you want per-user pricing, iAuditor or SimPro are the right picks; the comparison page explains where each fits.</p>",
